hat man  stare hadn't left my mind as I walked  alone to the bus stop but logically I  didn't expect to see anything and I  didn't run into anyone on the way to the  bus stop when I boarded the bus I made  sure there were no shady-looking  characters hiding in the back and once  again took one of the sideways facing  seats near the front  that's when maybe the most haunting part  of any of this became a reality looking  at the window I saw the same man from  before staring at me from beside the bus  standing right at the bus stop where I'd  been standing moments before I have no  idea how he could have tracked me from  her old apartments to her new apartment  and now to the bus stop miles away from  where this all started it seemed like  slow motion while the bus driver closed  the doors and the man made no attempt to  board his trenchcoat blowing in the wind  as he stared me all the way out of sight  that was the last time I saw the bus  creep in person since then I've woken up  three times tonight each time his face  was piercing into my nightmares I don't  think I'll be taking the bus tomorrow  [Music]  thanks for listening - Ahnold ain't a  creepypasta  your total today comes out to one dollar  and seventy five cents but if you like  this video right now I'll waive that fee  and give you everything you just listen  to absolutely free remember to subscribe  to see the world some new Horrors every  week bring that that Bell for  notifications  and I'll see you in the next one  assuming we survive

